            {
                "entry_id": "7dc3d469-cac6-343e-8c1e-50455e7b9a9c",
                "word": "gaff",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3e1dfbf2-ed54-403f-825e-7dcd458f2ff6",
                        "entry_id": "7dc3d469-cac6-343e-8c1e-50455e7b9a9c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gaffs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                        "entry_id": "7dc3d469-cac6-343e-8c1e-50455e7b9a9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A place of residence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "Ireland",
                            "Multicultural-London-English",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0c40009-51c6-46bf-83b3-342b20d0c66b",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "We're going round to Mike's gaff later to watch the footie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e14ea80c-b249-4a79-91ce-1bf2d3bf18b0",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "\"Steady on, mate. How was I to know this was your gaff? I was lookin' for somewhere to kip.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc42b126-2dec-4a9d-96a6-48df6aecfcd3",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "And like I said, I was so fuck-faced that I forgot I'd moved and let myself back into my old gaff."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2641774-5885-4af0-8a9a-661eb4d4e71b",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "Am I alone in feeling smug (if slatternly) about the news that super-clean homes are a breeding ground for infection? Apparently, all that bleach is bad not just for germs but for children's immune systems, too, and paradoxically causes more disease than it prevents. Not round my gaff. Oh no. My standards of housekeeping are so abysmally low that my eldest daughter was three years old before she even developed a temperature."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e5c98b9-eecc-4377-96a0-8a1858a078bf",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "Man will enter the gaf with crown\nGun shot spin his head right round"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd578ce7-817f-4a0c-b9f2-73d1092c4bb1",
                                "sense_id": "34b902b9-a984-3371-adc4-3ea3e45bfe1a",
                                "text": "The term ‘free gaf’ is music to any teenage ears in Dublin, while the term ‘wreak the gaf’ should fill any parent with dread. The term ‘gaf’ means ‘house,’ so when parents are away […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "057cd79c-6ae8-3c43-8df4-06fefae0607b",
                        "entry_id": "7dc3d469-cac6-343e-8c1e-50455e7b9a9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A disreputable, low-end theatre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62972f94-4136-42b2-8c4f-9f690208ab25",
                                "sense_id": "057cd79c-6ae8-3c43-8df4-06fefae0607b",
                                "text": "Significantly, the setting is a gaff, a low, illegal theatre, and not one of the legitimate East-End stages."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
